  "model": {
    "description": "Partial reconstruction of Level-0 definitions and scoped physical, chemical, biochemical, optical, retinal, visual and neural evidence. Levels organize the display; they do not establish a universal emergence order. Formal specifications, computational models, experimental preparations, observations and conditional interpretations have distinct roles. Each scientific claim retains its reviewed sources, selected system, observable, uncertainty, shared inputs and unresolved limitations. Field and particle models remain distinct from detector response, lattice calculations and conditional parameter extraction. Nuclear and atomic masses, primordial abundances and cosmological spectra retain their source-specific calibration, model and covariance limits. Atomic and molecular binding, prepared-state spectroscopy, charge production, electrolyte screening and stationary electronic representations address different questions; their energy comparisons do not by themselves establish formation kinetics, universal stability or a unique ancestry. Optical and neural records distinguish measured response from anatomy, intervention and theoretical interpretation. Behavioral success and fitted models do not identify a unique mechanism. Finite checks reproduce only their declared data or mathematical witnesses, not entire experiments. Cross-domain construction, universal parent weights and carrier minima, downward causation and a derivation of quantum theory from Level 0 remain unestablished. Source discrepancies and unreproduced stages remain explicit. No whole-graph scientific validation is claimed.",
    "id": "causal-emergence",
    "name": "Causal Emergence — Canonical Reconstruction",
    "status": "research-reconstruction-partial",
    "version": "2026.10.20.2"
  },
